---
description: company-ai project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Read SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md before any task. It is the source of truth. If a request conflicts with it, say so instead of silently deviating.

- Stack: Node.js, Express, TypeScript (strict), Zod, pino, Vitest, npm. Do not add dependencies without saying why.
- Layers: routes -> controllers -> services -> guardrails. One file, one job, aim for 150 lines or fewer.
- Keep code clean and understandable: explicit names, no clever abstractions, comments explain why. The owner must understand every line.
- Config only through validated env (src/config/env.ts). Never hardcode secrets or URLs.
- Never use console.log; use the pino logger. Never log passwords or tokens.
- Do only what the task asks. No extra features, no refactors outside the task.
- When finished: run typecheck, lint and tests, then give a short plain-English walkthrough of each new file (what it does, why each import exists) and list anything you were unsure about.
